"""English legal notices for the current static, free-download site.
Operator-specific placeholders must be completed before these become final notices.
"""
BOX='<span class="personal-info">[aqui tu informacion personal]</span>'
DATE='<p class="quiet">Last updated: 11 October 2026</p>'
DRAFT='<aside class="legal-note"><strong>Operator details pending.</strong> The highlighted fields must be completed by the website operator. These notices are drafts until the identifying and service-provider information is complete.</aside>'
def wrap(title,body):
    return '<section class="prose page-heading"><h1>'+title+'</h1>'+DATE+DRAFT+body+'</section>'
def operator():
    return '<dl class="operator-details">'+''.join('<dt>'+label+'</dt><dd>'+BOX+'</dd>' for label in ['Legal name / business name','Contact email','Postal address for legal notices (including country)','Tax identification number, where required','Registration details, if applicable (otherwise state “Not applicable”)'])+'</dl>'
PAGES=[
('/legal/','Legal Notice | Patrick’s Little Studio','Website operator details, hosting information and legal contact.',wrap('Legal notice',
    '<h2>Who operates this website?</h2><p>Patrick’s Little Studio is the public name of this coloring-page project. The legally responsible operator is identified below. Patrick, the studio character, is not the legal operator.</p>'+operator()+
    '<h2>What the website provides</h2><p>The website offers free printable mandalas, coloring suggestions and PDF downloads for personal and classroom activities. This version has no paid checkout, subscription, account, public comments or user-upload facility. It is not an accredited educational service, and does not offer medical or therapeutic advice.</p>'+
    '<h2>Hosting</h2><p>The public website is hosted on GitHub Pages. GitHub documents that visitors’ IP addresses are logged and stored for security, whether or not they are signed in. Read the <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub General Privacy Statement</a> and our <a href="/privacy/">privacy notice</a> for information on data handling.</p>'+
    '<h2>Creative identity</h2><p>Patrick is a fictional studio character whose portrait was generated with AI. The project and downloadable collection are real; the character is not presented as evidence of a real person’s qualifications or professional experience. Details of the creative process appear on <a href="/about/">About the studio</a>.</p>'+
    '<h2>Legal and intellectual-property enquiries</h2><p>Contact the operator at the email above. For a rights concern, identify the relevant page or file, the material concerned, your relationship to the rights holder and a way to respond. Do not include unnecessary sensitive data. A report will be reviewed; submitting it does not automatically establish infringement.</p>'+
    '<h2>Applicable rules</h2><p>The project is intended to be operated from Spain. Where applicable, the operator’s activities are subject to Spanish rules, including Law 34/2002 on information-society services, EU data-protection law and Spain’s Organic Law 3/2018. Mandatory protections in other jurisdictions remain applicable when their legal conditions are met. These notices do not assert universal legal compliance.</p>')),
('/privacy/','Privacy Notice | Patrick’s Little Studio','How the website handles hosting data, contact messages and children’s privacy.',wrap('Privacy notice',
    '<aside class="child-summary"><strong>For children and families:</strong> You can choose and download a drawing without giving us your name or creating an account. There are no ads, chat rooms or upload buttons. The company hosting the website receives technical information to deliver and protect it. Ask an adult before sending an email; do not send children’s names, photos or school details.</aside>'+
    '<h2>1. Controller and contact</h2><p>The operator below is responsible for personal information they receive and decide how to use. GitHub also processes technical data for its own hosting and security purposes as described in its statement.</p>'+operator()+
    '<h2>2. Data and purposes</h2><div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Situation</th><th>Information</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Opening a page or PDF</td><td>IP address and technical request information processed by the hosting service</td><td>Deliver content, operate the service and maintain security</td></tr><tr><td>Emailing the operator</td><td>Email address, name if supplied, message and attachments</td><td>Answer the enquiry, investigate a reported problem or handle a rights request</td></tr><tr><td>Legal obligations or disputes</td><td>Relevant correspondence and limited supporting records</td><td>Meet applicable obligations and establish, exercise or defend legal claims</td></tr></tbody></table></div>'+
    '<p>The studio does not add visitor analytics, advertising pixels, fingerprinting, mailing-list software or profiling. It does not buy personal information or use download details for advertising. There is no automated decision-making with legal or similarly significant effects. Supplying an email is voluntary and is not required to download a drawing. Without contact information, an enquiry may not be answerable.</p>'+
    '<h2>3. Legal bases</h2><p>For correspondence handled by the operator, the basis under EU GDPR Article 6(1)(f), and UK GDPR where applicable, is the legitimate interest in answering requests, keeping the service secure and resolving issues, subject to the individual’s rights and reasonable expectations. Records necessary to meet a specific legal obligation rely on Article 6(1)(c). Handling legal claims may rely on legitimate interests and applicable legal requirements. Visiting a page is not consent to marketing. GitHub’s own legal bases for its processing are set out in its privacy statement.</p>'+
    '<h2>4. Recipients and service providers</h2><p>The public host is GitHub. If you email the operator, the operator’s email provider will process the message; authorised professional advisers or competent authorities may receive relevant information when necessary for a legal matter. The operator does not publish incoming messages or sell personal data. The email service provider and its privacy notice must be identified here:</p><p>'+BOX+'</p>'+
    '<h2>5. International processing</h2><p>GitHub operates internationally and may process information outside the EEA or UK. Its statement explains the jurisdictions and transfer mechanisms it uses, including applicable adequacy frameworks and contractual safeguards. See <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub’s privacy statement</a>. The operator’s email provider, processing locations and applicable transfer safeguard, if any, must also be recorded here:</p><p>'+BOX+'</p><p>You may contact the operator for further information and a copy of applicable safeguards, subject to lawful redaction. This notice does not claim that all data remains in Europe.</p>'+
    '<h2>6. Retention</h2><p>The operator keeps ordinary enquiries only for as long as needed to answer them and complete necessary follow-up, then deletes them or removes identifying details. Records connected with an unresolved dispute, rights request or legal obligation may be kept for the relevant statutory period or until the matter and any applicable claim period end. Provider-operated security logs and backups follow the provider’s own retention practices; the operator does not set or promise a retention period for GitHub’s logs.</p>'+
    '<h2>7. Your rights</h2><p>Where the relevant law applies, you may request access, correction, deletion or restriction, and data portability where its conditions are met. You may withdraw consent for any future consent-based processing without affecting prior lawful processing.</p><p><strong>Right to object:</strong> You may object to processing based on legitimate interests for reasons relating to your situation. We must consider the objection under the applicable rules; some records may lawfully need to be retained.</p><p>Send requests to the operator’s contact email. Provide only the information reasonably needed to identify the records and verify the request. EU and UK GDPR requests are normally answered within one month; a lawful extension of up to two further months will be explained within the initial period. Requests are generally free, subject to applicable exceptions. For data controlled independently by GitHub, use its privacy contact channels.</p>'+
    '<p>You may complain to the <a href="https://www.aepd.es/">Spanish Data Protection Agency (AEPD)</a>, another competent EEA supervisory authority, or the <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/">UK Information Commissioner’s Office</a> where applicable, without first contacting us.</p>'+
    '<h2>8. Children</h2><p>The drawings are designed for children, while downloads and printing can be managed by parents and teachers. We do not ask children to register, submit artwork, send photos or provide personal information. Technical information needed to deliver and secure the site is still handled by the host. The operator does not use it to build children’s profiles or for behavioral advertising.</p><p>Do not send a child’s personal details, image, voice, location or school information by email. If the operator learns that unnecessary information about a child has been received, they will remove it, except where a specific legal obligation requires retention. Parents or guardians may contact the operator about information concerning their child.</p><p>No blanket age disclaimer replaces duties under US COPPA, EU/UK data protection or other applicable children’s privacy rules. Before introducing data collection, advertising, accounts, uploads or social features, the operator must assess age-related safeguards and any parental notice or verifiable consent requirements.</p>'+
    '<h2>9. US and other visitors</h2><p>The operator does not sell personal information or share it for cross-context behavioral advertising. State and national privacy rights apply where their legal scope and thresholds are met; this notice does not claim that the operator meets every US state-law threshold. You may contact the operator to request access, correction or deletion where available. Exercising a privacy right will not affect access to the free drawings.</p>'+
    '<h2>10. Security and updates</h2><p>HTTPS and the hosting platform’s security measures protect delivery. No website or email system can guarantee absolute security. Please avoid sending confidential or sensitive information. If data uses or providers change, the notice will be updated before the new processing begins, with additional notice or consent where required.</p>')),
('/cookies/','Cookies & Storage | Patrick’s Little Studio','Information about cookies, browser storage and the current tracking-free studio implementation.',wrap('Cookies & browser storage',
    '<h2>What the studio adds</h2><p>The current public website does not add cookies, local storage, session storage, advertising tags, embedded social media or visitor analytics. Images, fonts and PDF downloads do not require a studio account. Opening the privacy notice or downloading a file does not mean you consent to optional tracking.</p>'+
    '<h2>Hosting and technical information</h2><p>GitHub Pages handles network requests and records IP addresses for security. Technical server logs are not the same as cookies. The hosting provider’s own practices are explained in the <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub privacy statement</a>. Links to external websites take you to their services, which may use their own cookies.</p>'+
    '<h2>Consent choices</h2><p>No optional cookie categories are enabled by the studio in this version, so there are no optional studio cookies to accept or reject. If non-essential storage or tracking is added later, it must remain disabled until any legally required consent is obtained. Accept and reject choices must be clear and equally easy, and withdrawal must be available. Continued browsing will not be treated as consent.</p>'+
    '<h2>Your browser</h2><p>You can inspect and delete site data through your browser settings. Downloaded PDFs and cached images are files handled by your browser; deleting cookies does not delete a PDF you saved. If a future hosting configuration introduces additional cookies, this notice and any necessary controls must be updated.</p><p>Questions: contact the operator listed in the <a href="/legal/">legal notice</a>.</p>')),
('/terms/','Terms & Printing Licence | Patrick’s Little Studio','Conditions for free mandala downloads, personal and classroom printing, sharing and rights enquiries.',wrap('Terms & printing licence',
    '<h2>1. Operator and scope</h2><p>These terms describe permitted uses of the studio’s materials and website. The responsible operator and contact details appear in the <a href="/legal/">legal notice</a>. The privacy notice is information about data handling, not consent obtained merely by accepting these terms. Statutory rights remain unaffected.</p>'+
    '<h2>2. Free personal and classroom use</h2><p>To the extent the operator holds rights capable of being licensed, permission is granted to download, print, color and adapt the provided mandalas for personal, family, school and other non-commercial group coloring activities. Teachers may print copies for their classes and share the files privately with pupils or parents for those activities. You may share photographs of your own colored results, subject to the rights and privacy of anyone shown.</p><p>No purchase, account or subscription is required. Your internet provider, paper and printing costs remain your responsibility.</p>'+
    '<h2>3. Redistribution and commercial uses</h2><p>Please link to the original design page when recommending an uncolored drawing publicly. The permission above does not include reselling the files, including them in a paid download pack, printing merchandise for sale, or republishing the uncolored collection as your own downloadable catalog. For uses beyond this permission, contact the operator. These conditions do not restrict uses independently permitted by law or impose exclusive rights where none exist.</p>'+
    '<h2>4. Rights and AI-assisted material</h2><p>The artwork and Patrick portrait were generated with AI from project-specific briefs; the site also contains text, layout, selection and other material. Copyright protection for AI-generated elements varies by jurisdiction and depends on the facts. The studio does not claim exclusive ownership of every machine-generated shape or guarantee that each element is protectable. Third-party rights, including trademarks and personality rights, remain unaffected.</p><p>Your coloring does not transfer any rights you may hold in your own creative contribution to the operator. Report a suspected rights issue through the legal contact with the relevant URL and supporting details.</p>'+
    '<h2>5. Responsible use</h2><p>Do not interfere with the service, attempt unauthorised access, use it for unlawful activity, misrepresent your identity, or infringe others’ rights. Printing and coloring are intended as creative activities. Adults should choose suitable materials and supervise children when needed; the pages are not professional educational, therapeutic or safety advice.</p>'+
    '<h2>6. Availability and limitations</h2><p>We aim to provide usable files, but availability, printer output and display may vary. The operator may correct, replace or remove a file where reasonably necessary, including for safety or rights concerns. No claim is made that the service will always be uninterrupted or error-free.</p><p>Nothing here excludes liability that cannot lawfully be excluded, including liability for fraud, deliberate misconduct or other mandatory protections. Any limitation applies only to the extent allowed by applicable law; consumers retain non-waivable rights. These terms do not impose a blanket waiver of all claims.</p>'+
    '<h2>7. External links</h2><p>External services have their own terms and data practices. A link does not transfer control of those services to the studio or remove obligations the operator may have under applicable law.</p>'+
    '<h2>8. Changes</h2><p>Updated terms will show a new revision date and apply prospectively, subject to applicable law. Where a change requires active agreement or specific notice, posting the update alone will not replace that requirement. No change retrospectively removes mandatory rights or permissions already exercised lawfully.</p>'+
    '<h2>9. Law and disputes</h2><p>Spanish law governs these terms to the extent permissible, without depriving consumers of mandatory protections available under the law of their habitual residence where applicable. Courts and jurisdiction are determined by applicable law; there is no compulsory arbitration clause or blanket exclusive Spanish-court requirement for all international visitors.</p><p>Contact the operator first if you wish to seek an informal resolution. This is optional and does not limit complaint rights, remedies or access to a competent authority or court.</p>'))
]
